SUMMARY:Science TODAY: When Wild Animals Meet People
DESCRIPTION:Understanding Human-Carnivore Conflict in China\nGo inside the globe of the SECU Daily Planet Theater for live presentations and interactive shows led by scientists and educators. Meet researchers\, witness live demonstrations\, and engage in Q&A sessions with experts. With ever-changing topics and guests\, there’s always something new and exciting to learn. \nToday’s Topic \nWhat happens when people and large carnivores share the same landscape? Using 520 reported conflict events across China\, this talk explores where conflicts occur\, why they happen\, and how people and wildlife can coexist. \nToday’s Expert \nJiahui Yuan\, Tsinghua University & Biodiversity lab\, North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/science-today-when-wild-animals-meet-people/
LOCATION:Nature Research Center\, 121 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,All Ages,Children,Discussions,Lectures,SECU Daily Planet Theater,Teens,Walk-up Programs
ORGANIZER;CN="Chris%20Smith":MAILTO:christopher.smith@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822405;-78.6409677
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Nature Research Center 121 West Jones Street Raleigh NC 27601 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=121 West Jones Street:geo:-78.6409677,35.7822405
